  "result": "I added `wrapText(text, width)` to `src/cli/wrap.ts` and committed it. The 6 new tests pass, and `tsc` and biome are clean. I did not run the full `npm run fast` or `npm run gate`, and the commit has no task id or `Ticket:` trailer.\n\n- **Wrapping:** it fills each line greedily up to `width`. A word that is no longer than `width` is never split, so it moves to the next line instead. A word longer than `width` is hard-split into `width`-sized chunks.\n- **Whitespace:** runs of whitespace collapse to a single space, and empty or whitespace-only text returns `[]`.\n- **Invalid width:** a width that isn't a positive integer throws a `RangeError`.\n- **Tests:** they are in `test/cli/wrap.test.ts`.\n- **Notes:** the plan and status are in `docs/wrap-text-notes.md`, written before the code, with every step now ticked off.",
